<article class="env-lemma" id="0385">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0385">Lemma <span data-tag="0385">33.7.4</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$, $Y$ be schemes over $k$. Assume $X$ is geometrically connected over $k$. Then the projection morphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  p : X \times _ k Y \longrightarrow Y  \]
</div>
  <p> induces a bijection between connected components. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The scheme theoretic fibres of $p$ are connected, since they are base changes of the geometrically connected scheme $X$ by field extensions. Moreover the scheme theoretic fibres are homeomorphic to the set theoretic fibres, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01K1" data-tag="01K1">26.18.5</a>. By Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0383" data-tag="0383">29.24.4</a> the map $p$ is open. Thus we may apply Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0378" data-tag="0378">5.7.6</a> to conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>